Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:03:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Docker reachability and preserve data across container
 recreation

Serve the existing Flask app through one threaded Waitress process bound to
all container interfaces, with a persistent /data volume. Preserve direct
Python startup defaults and add an optional data-directory environment setting.

Run the image as a non-root user with health checks and explicit Compose
network/storage controls. Document migration and trusted LAN configuration.

Exercise upstream API/auth/operation suites against an isolated host port and
verify score and file persistence after container removal/recreation. Configure
a Docker integration workflow without adding publication or deployment.

Validated locally: 28 API checks, authentication/operation suites, and the
container recreation test all pass using a Docker-compatible Podman image.
